timestamp=2026-07-13T20:20:59.896Z level=INFO run=005dc7fd message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > /home/johncoffee/growth-log/2026-07-13.md << 'EOF'\n## RSA Signature Bypass via Binary Patching\n\n### Context\n- Needed to flash a modified VBIOS onto an AMD Radeon Pro VII (Vega20)\n- amdvbflash v4.71 has RSA signature verification that rejects modified ROMs\n- The `-f` flag skips version/SSID checks but RSA still blocks\n\n### Root Cause / Core Insight\n- The \"BIOS authentication signature mismatched\" error comes from RSA verification functions at VA 0x424314 and 0x416ea5\n- Patched the ELF64 binary directly: changed conditional jumps (`jne`→`jmp`, `jne`→`nop`), return values (`mov $0x0,%ebp`→`mov $0x1,%ebp`), and error codes (`0x25`→`0x24`) across 12 locations\n- The RSA verification has multiple fallback paths (8 error call sites) - all must be patched\n\n### The Pattern (transferable)\n- Next time I need to bypass binary signature checks, I will: (1) disassemble with objdump, (2) find the verification functions, (3) trace all conditional jumps to error paths, (4) patch every failure path to turn into success paths\n- Signal to recognize: error code 0xFL01 / \"authentication signature mismatched\" in AMD/ATI flash tools\n\n### Related\n- The original ROM was at /mnt/win1/123\\ tranqueiras\\ e\\ projetos/projeto\\ bios\\ mod/bios\\ mi50/277846.rom\n- amdvbflash v4.71 binary at /tmp/amdvbflash_patched\n- Fully patched binary at /tmp/amdvbflash_patched_norsa\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
